From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] relay: key the multicast duplicate check on {origin, MID}, not MID alone

A foreign agent joined our mesh over the backhaul, its 1905 reached our
agents in both directions - and our CONTROLLER never saw a single frame from
it. Measured 2026-09-21 with tcpdump on the controller's br-lan
(ether proto 0x893a, 40 s):

    33x  hall       -> MTK        19x  MTK -> hall
     5x  MTK -> corridor           5x  MTK -> kitchen
     0x  controller <-> MTK

The controller is the registrar. Without it the agent never gets its WSC M2,
so it keeps its own SSID and the mesh is not one network. Nothing about the
radio or WPS was wrong - the frames were dropped on the way.

Relayed multicast is deduplicated per outgoing interface against the last
four MIDs seen. A MID is a per-sender counter, so two senders reach the same
value all the time, and then a perfectly good frame from one is dropped
because the other used that MID a moment earlier. With a foreign vendor this
stops being a coincidence: its counter is seeded independently of ours and
sweeps across our range.

The window makes it worse. Four entries are one per node in a four-node mesh,
so a single round of Topology Query/Response fills it and everything later is
matched against a ring that has already turned over.

So key on {origin AL-MAC, MID}, which is what a duplicate means, and give the
window room. The origin is already in scope: it is handed to i1905_cmdu_tx as
the source of the relayed frame two lines below.

The hardcoded 4 in the index wrap goes too. It is the same constant only by
accident, and the next person to widen the window would have found the array
growing while the ring still turned over after four entries.

Upstream marks this block "#if 1 //TODO: improve" - an acknowledged stub, not
a considered design.

Measured before the change so there is something to compare against:
multi-hop relaying works (controller -> hall -> corridor/kitchen, and the
foreign box reaches every agent). That is what must not regress.

diff -u -r a/src/i1905.c b/src/i1905.c
--- a/src/i1905.c
+++ b/src/i1905.c
@@ -785,10 +785,21 @@
 		if (ifname && !strncmp(ifname, ifs->ifname, 16))
 			continue;
 
-#if 1	//TODO: improve
+		/* A duplicate is the same MID from the same originator. Keyed on
+		 * the MID alone this dropped every frame whose sender had picked
+		 * a MID one of the others used moments earlier - which is how a
+		 * foreign agent's 1905 reached our agents and never reached the
+		 * controller (measured 2026-09-21, tcpdump on br-lan: 33 frames
+		 * hall<->MTK, 0 controller<->MTK).
+		 */
+		{
+		static const uint8_t noorigin[6] = { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
+		const uint8_t *origin = src ? src : noorigin;
+
 		dup = false;
 		for (i = 0; i < I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX; i++) {
-			if (ifpriv->lastmid[i] == mid) {
+			if (ifpriv->lastmid[i].mid == mid &&
+			    !memcmp(ifpriv->lastmid[i].origin, origin, 6)) {
 				dup = true;
 				break;
 			}
@@ -797,9 +808,15 @@
 		if (dup)
 			continue;
 
-		ifpriv->lastmid[ifpriv->lastmid_idx] = mid;
-		ifpriv->lastmid_idx = (ifpriv->lastmid_idx + 1) % 4;
-#endif
+		memcpy(ifpriv->lastmid[ifpriv->lastmid_idx].origin, origin, 6);
+		ifpriv->lastmid[ifpriv->lastmid_idx].mid = mid;
+		/* the wrap used a hardcoded 4; widening the window above would
+		 * otherwise have grown the array while the ring still turned
+		 * over after four entries.
+		 */
+		ifpriv->lastmid_idx =
+			(ifpriv->lastmid_idx + 1) % I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX;
+		}
 		ret = i1905_cmdu_tx(ifpriv, ifs->vid, dst, src, type, &mid,
 				     frm->data, frm->datalen, false);
 		if (ret < 0) {
diff -u -r a/src/i1905.h b/src/i1905.h
--- a/src/i1905.h
+++ b/src/i1905.h
@@ -75,8 +75,20 @@
 	bool registrar;
 	bool configured;
 
-#define I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX	4
-	uint16_t lastmid[I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX];
+/* Remembering a MID alone drops good frames: a MID is a per-sender counter,
+ * so two senders collide on it routinely, and a foreign vendor's counter runs
+ * independently of ours. The duplicate that matters is the same MID from the
+ * same originator.
+ *
+ * Four entries were also one per node in a four-node mesh - a single round of
+ * Topology Query/Response turned the ring over. Sixteen costs 128 bytes per
+ * interface and survives a busy round.
+ */
+#define I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX	16
+	struct i1905_relay_seen {
+		uint8_t origin[6];
+		uint16_t mid;
+	} lastmid[I1905_MID_LOOKBACK_MAX];
 	int lastmid_idx;
 	struct i1905_interface_private_wsc *wsc;
 
